  "notes": "West's opening heart lead goes to the ♥A. East returns the ♥Q and it looks natural for South to try to win the ♥K. If West is able to ruff, he will return a diamond through North's tenace putting the contract at risk.\n\nIf South ducks at trick 2 the contract is almost certain. West will discard and East will continue hearts giving West a ruff. South can win West's diamond shift in dummy and ruff a heart.\n\nAfter drawing trump North has a club winner and a heart winner to take care of South's losing diamonds. Dummy has an entry in clubs to reach these winners.",
